      "writtenOn": "2025-08-13T20:35:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unrelated to this change, but historically functions prefixed with `board_` were used to create weak overrides and allow board specific code to modify behavior.\n\nIt looks like both `led_gpio` and `led_pwm` define this function which implies that GPIO and PWM style LEDs are mutually exclusive.\n\nBecause this is only required for PWM, it would be better to guard the call and only define for PWM configs.\n\n```\nled_tick()\n    led_set_all_colors(); /* board_led_set_color() renamed */\n    if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_LED_DT_PWM))\n        led_pwm_apply_color();\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 168,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 168,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "a7a384efa7919b0f41333571f94cf706154e9225",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
